The issue is fixed by ensuring that google maps is only called once. 


In the restaurant overlay, whenever it is triggered, it the script tries to load the script

`<script id="google-maps-script" src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=<KEY>&amp;libraries=places" async=""></script>`

When this is loaded twice, the overlay doesn’t open anymore, thus map is not rendered too. 

To fix this, added a check to see if the script is already loaded to the browser. If it’s the first time, load the script, otherwise skip. 

```
if (window.google && window.google.maps) {
      resolve();
      return;
    }
```

