## Bug Fix Summary

This PR fixes a null pointer exception in FormHandler.js that was causing the application to crash.

### Issue Fixed
- **Location**: Line 2 in `server/FormHandler.js`
- **Problem**: Code was accessing `data.field.length` without checking if `data` or `data.field` exists
- **Error**: Runtime crash when null/undefined data is passed

### Solution
- Added proper null/undefined validation before accessing nested properties
- Implemented graceful error handling with fallback message
- Prevents application crashes while maintaining functionality

### Code Changes
```javascript
// Before (vulnerable to null pointer)
console.log(data.field.length);

// After (safe with validation)
if (data && data.field && typeof data.field.length !== 'undefined') {
  console.log(data.field.length);
} else {
  console.log('Field data is not available or invalid');
}
```

### Testing
The fix has been tested with:
- Valid data with field property
- Null/undefined data
- Data without field property

All scenarios now handle gracefully without crashing.

